{
  "raw": {
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53089": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty - Reference &amp; Electronic Resources Librarian",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Regular Faculty - Reference &amp; Electronic Resources Librarian Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regular Faculty - Reference & Electronic Resources Librarian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001447P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Regular Faculty - Reference & Electronic Resources Librarian Advertising Pay Range $65,000 annually or higher commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Law Primary Unit Law Library Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Regular Faculty Position Control Number 4483 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 01/04/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Negotiable (must be justified) Rank Negotiable (must be justified) Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary This is a full-time (fiscal year appointment) tenure-track or tenured position for the College of Law’s Moscow location, at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Rank and tenure are negotiable based on how the candidate meets the criteria outlined in department and college bylaws. The faculty member in this position will be an integral part of the Law Library and legal research faculty team, working under the supervision and general direction of the Director of the Law Library. This faculty member will be responsible for the Law Library’s electronic resources management, policies, and decisions. Duties include, but are not limited to: 1) supervising the maintenance of Law Library-specific electronic databases and resources, including LibGuides, Digital Commons, and vendor study aid subscriptions; 2) working closely with the University Library to coordinate the Law Library’s participation in the shared integrated library system; 3) coordinating the Law Library’s compliance with Title II digital accessibility requirements. In addition, this position provides reference and research support to College of Law students, faculty, and staff, as well as to members of the University community and the general public; and teaches Introduction to Legal Research and other potential courses. The faculty member will also conduct outreach, attend faculty meetings, and serve on committees at the University and/or College level. The University of Idaho College of Law maintains two campuses in Moscow and Boise. The Law Library administers and manages the Idaho State Law Library pursuant to a Memorandum of Understanding with the Idaho Supreme Court. The Law Library is a member of the Orbis Cascade Alliance, a consortium of 37 academic libraries in Washington, Oregon, and Idaho, with access to over 28 million items. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/law Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 70% Scholarship & Creative Activity 10% Outreach & Extension 10% University Service & Leadership 10% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Required Qualifications JD from ABA -accredited school and Successful completion of at least one year of an MLIS program from an ALA -accredited school, or equivalent experience Teaching experience or related experience Preferred Qualifications Completion of an MLIS program Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 09/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The priority consideration date will be 10/25/26. Required documents for application are (1) Resume/CV; (2) Letter of Qualification addressing whether you satisfy each of the required and preferred qualifications for the position; (3) List of three references; (4) Research agenda describing your scholarly interests and anticipated future research projects (upload to Other Document 1 field); (5) Statement describing any Bar disciplinary history (if applicable) (upload to Other Document 2 field). Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53087": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty - Mathematics and Statistical Science",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Regular Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regular Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001460P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Regular Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Science Primary Unit Mathematics and Statistical Science Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Regular Faculty Position Control Number 8197 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Department of Mathematics and Statistical Science is seeking to hire a new tenure-track applied mathematician or statistician at the Assistant Professor level at the Moscow campus. Potential research areas may include (but are not limited to) mathematical and computational modeling, mathematical biology, biostatistics, statistical methodology, machine learning, or other quantitative approaches relevant to health and biomedical research. This position will be secondarily affiliated with the university’s NIH -funded COBRE in Nutrition and Women’s Health. As such, successful candidates should be interested in and willing to collaborate with other university faculty conducting research related to nutrition and women’s health as well as participate in COBRE in Nutrition and Women’s Health activities. Instructional duties include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in mathematics and/or statistics (typically two courses per semester) to support mathematics and statistics education at the university and the BS, MS, and PhD programs. Mentoring and advising students are expected. Scholarship duties include conducting research in applied mathematics or statistics, disseminating research through publications in refereed professional journals, and seeking external funding to support research activities. Service duties include serving on departmental and university committees and participating in recruitment and retention efforts. Outreach duties include participating in activities related to community involvement and serving in the professional community. The College of Science is also recruiting new faculty in biology (ecological immunology), geography (health geography), geology (critical materials), physics (research area open), and statistics or applied mathematics (for independent or collaborative research in nutrition and women’s health). Applications from partners or collaborators who fit these positions are encouraged. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/science/academics/mathematics-statistical-science Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 50% Scholarship & Creative Activity 40% Outreach & Extension 5% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Mathematics, Statistics, or a related field Record of research activity in applied mathematics or statistics Experience teaching mathematics and/or statistics or as a teaching assistant at the university level Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral research experience Demonstrated grant writing experience History of peer-reviewed publications in mathematics, statistics, or related fields Experience teaching mathematics and/or statistics at the university level Experience working as part of a multidisciplinary team Experience in developing and/or applying mathematical or statistical methods to research in nutrition and/or women’s health Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/11/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants As part of the application, you will need to provide a cover letter and both a statement of teaching and a statement of research. Your cover letter (maximum of two single-spaced pages) should address how you meet each qualification. Your statement of research (maximum of two single-spaced pages) should include a discussion of your research experience and interests, experience applying for funding, plans for future research programs, and plans for funding for your research. Include connections to your past and/or future research on nutrition and/or women’s health. Your statement of teaching (maximum of two single-spaced pages) should include a discussion of your teaching experiences, methods, style, and innovations. Please be sure to include concrete examples in your statement. This position will remain open until filled, however, applications received on or before November 15, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho will not be supported until further notice.  Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Transcripts Statement of Research Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
