    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53080": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty - Civil & Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001458P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Engineering Primary Unit Civil & Environmental Engineering Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 2994 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Idaho invites applications for an academic year, full-time, clinical (non-tenure-track) faculty position. We welcome applications from candidates with expertise in any area of civil engineering whose teaching, research, and professional experience would complement and strengthen our programs. Preference may be given to candidates with expertise in structural engineering and/or significant professional experience in industry or professional practice. Structural engineering is a vital foundation of civil engineering and provides opportunities to contribute to a broad range of core undergraduate courses. We also value the perspective that professional experience brings to the classroom and the opportunities to engage with industry. The successful candidate will be an outstanding educator capable of teaching foundational engineering courses, such as Statics, Mechanics of Materials, Fluid Mechanics, Engineering Surveying, Drafting, and Civil Engineering Analysis and Design. The successful candidate will also have opportunities to advise and mentor undergraduate students, both academically and through student organizations such as the American Society of Civil Engineers ( ASCE ) student chapter. We are committed to providing a high-quality education through teaching excellence and to fostering a productive, collaborative, and collegial environment where students, faculty, and staff can thrive. Unit/Department Summary Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering | University of Idaho Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 90% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 0% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications B.S. in Civil Engineering and M.S. in Civil Engineering or closely related field Experience communicating both orally and in writing. Ability to obtain licensure as a Professional Engineer (PE) in Idaho within 5 years of hire. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. in Civil Engineering or closely related field Demonstrated excellence in teaching undergraduate courses in area of expertise Demonstrated ability to collaborate in interdisciplinary environments Professional experience in private practice or public agency Currently hold a Professional Engineer (PE) license Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/11/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open until filled with first consideration being given to completed applications submitted by December 1, 2026. A complete application consists of a CV, letter of application, teaching statement, and list of at least 3 references. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho is supported in limited circumstances from existing visa holders. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data,