    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53071": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty - Earth and Spatial Sciences",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001455P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience. Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Science Primary Unit Earth and Spatial Sciences Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 4575 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary This academic year non-tenured track Assistant Professor faculty member is expected to teach courses in geology according to the needs of the department and as directed by the department chair. This position will expand externally funded research, strengthen industry and national laboratory partnerships, and further establish the University of Idaho as a statewide and regional leader in mining-related research and innovation. Critical minerals, which include lithium, cobalt, rare earth elements, and other strategically important resources, are a major national priority and an area of significant investment by federal agencies, including the Department of Energy ( DOE ), National Science Foundation ( NSF ), and Department of Defense ( DOD ). A clinical faculty member in this area would position the university to compete for these investments while developing sustained partnerships with national laboratories, industry, and other universities. This position will include the role as Director of the Electron Microscopy Center and will sustain and expand its Mission, including instruction on specialized equipment. Building these long-term programs and partnerships requires continuity, research leadership, and institutional commitment. The College of Science is also recruiting new faculty in biology (ecological immunology), geography (health geography), geology (critical materials), physics (research area open), and statistics or applied mathematics (for independent or collaborative research in nutrition and women’s health). Unit/Department Summary Department of Earth and Spatial Sciences | University of Idaho Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 50% Scholarship & Creative Activity 20% Outreach & Extension 5% University Service & Leadership 25% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Geology or other geosciences related field Expertise in geology, as indicated by dissertation research, peer-reviewed publications, and/or industry experience Experience in developing externally funded research program Expertise in analysis using an Electron microscopy equipment including – XRD , SEM , Crystallographer Preferred Qualifications Experience in teaching graduate and undergraduate mineralogy and petrology courses, or additional needs of the department Demonstrated scholarship and teaching excellence in mineralogy, or critical minerals, or a related field Potential for collaborative research with UI faculty Excellent written and oral communication skills Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Must be able to lift, carry and/or otherwise move 30 pounds Posting Information Posting Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position will remain open until filled, however, applications received on or before November 15, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho is supported in limited circumstances from existing visa holders. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Research/Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53068": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty - Physics",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Regular Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regular Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001454P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Regular Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Science Primary Unit Physics Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Regular Faculty Position Control Number 0385 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. The department currently has faculty working on various topics in astrophysics, biophysics, condensed matter, nuclear and quantum physics, optics, and planetary science, and the college is pursuing initiatives in biomedical and bioengineering fields. All areas will be considered. Instructional duties for research active faculty typically include teaching one three-credit hour course per semester at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. These courses support university-wide physics education, as well as B.A., B.S., M.S. and Ph.D. programs in physics. The new faculty member will be expected to mentor undergraduate and graduate students in the physics program. Scholarship duties include conducting research in physics, disseminating research through publications in refereed professional journals and presentations at conferences, and seeking external funding to support research activities. Outreach duties include participating in activities related to community involvement and serving the professional physics community through scholarship. Service duties include serving on department, college and/or university-level committees. The College of Science is also recruiting new faculty in biology (ecological immunology), geography (health geography), geology (critical materials), and statistics or applied mathematics (for independent or collaborative research in nutrition and women’s health). Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/science/academics/physics Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 35% Scholarship & Creative Activity 55% Outreach & Extension 5% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in physics or a closely related field. Record of research activity in physics, demonstrated by peer-reviewed publications Preferred Qualifications Evidence of productive post-doctoral or equivalent experience. Evidence of potential to acquire external funding, demonstrated by submitted and/or funded proposals. Evidence of ability to teach University of Idaho undergraduate and graduate physics courses Evidence of synergies with the existing research strengths in the department or college, described in the letter of application Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position will remain open until filled, however, applications received on or before November 15, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho will not be supported until further notice. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application Statement of Research Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
