    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/53065": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty - Earth and Spatial Sciences",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Regular Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regular Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001453P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Regular Faculty Advertising Pay Range COE Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Science Primary Unit Earth and Spatial Sciences Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Regular Faculty Position Control Number 4530 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary This academic year, tenure track, regular faculty assistant professor is expected to teach courses in health geography and GIS according to the needs of the department and as directed by the department chair. The faculty member will also serve as an advisor to undergraduates as directed by the department chair. The faculty member will also serve as an advisor to graduate students to sustain a competitive research program. The faculty member will conduct research in an Earth science or related discipline, publish such research in peer reviewed journals, present findings at professional conferences, and submit proposals to extramural competitive funding agencies to fund this work. The faculty member is expected to attend faculty meetings, and to participate in committees at the department level and the college or university level. The faculty member is expected to participate in some outreach activities as directed by their chair or dean. The faculty member is expected to complete annual trainings, submit grades, and provide student feedback in a timely manner. The College of Science is also recruiting new faculty in biology (ecological immunology), geography (health geography), geology (critical materials), physics (research area open), and statistics or applied mathematics (for independent or collaborative research in nutrition and women’s health). Unit/Department Summary www.uidaho.edu/sci/ess Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 40% Scholarship & Creative Activity 50% Outreach & Extension 5% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Geography or related field Experience in teaching graduate and undergraduate courses meeting the needs of the department Expertise in health geography and GIS , as indicated by dissertation research, peer-reviewed publications. Experience to develop an externally funded research program. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated scholarship and teaching excellence in geography or a related field Ability to teach GIS courses. Experience for collaborative research with UI faculty. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions N/A Posting Information Posting Date 10/09/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position will remain open until filled, however, applications received on or before November 9, 2026, will receive first consideration. Posting will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho will not be supported until further notice. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Research/Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
