    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52985": {
      "title": "**Interim Sustainability Certificate Director / VProvAI - Vice Provost for Academic Initiatives",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | **Interim Sustainability Certificate Director / VProvAI Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help **Interim Sustainability Certificate Director / VProvAI Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001450P Internal Posting? This Search is Open to Current University of Idaho Employees Only Recruitment Title **Interim Sustainability Certificate Director / VProvAI Advertising Pay Range AY faculty - 10% base salary stipend during AY 2026-27 + Summer 2027 contract receiving a 10% base salary stipend. FY faculty - 10% base salary stipend. Location Moscow Primary Division/College Vice Provost for Academic Initiatives Primary Unit Vice Provost for Academic Initiatives Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Program Dir/Dist Dir/Super Position Control Number 7307 Suffix 01 Contingency Code 5 FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 09/28/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Negotiable (must be justified) Rank Negotiable (must be justified) Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Interim Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) 08/13/2027 Position Responsibilities Position Summary N/A Unit/Department Summary Vice Provost for Academic Initiatives at the University of Idaho (uidaho.edu) Administrative Summary The Interim Director of the Sustainability Certificate is a one-year appointment terming at the end of Summer 2027 and will lead the administration of the university’s first all-college certificate. Sustainability is an interdisciplinary topic that has relevance in nearly every area of work and life, and the certificate is expected to grow rapidly. Certificate completion will allow students to contribute to an informed citizenry that is creating sustainable solutions for Idaho and beyond, and to cultivate an ecologically sound, economically prosperous, and equitable society for current and future generations. The Interim Director will play a critical role in advising students currently enrolled in the program and recruiting prospective students to the certificate. Fiscal year employees are encouraged to apply. Academic year faculty will receive a 10% base salary stipend and are required to continue the work until the end of Summer 2027 under summer contract. Fiscal year faculty will also receive a 10% base salary stipend and are required to complete the duties until the end of Summer 2027. The Interim Director will be responsible for: Providing leadership in designing, implementing, managing, and delivering the university’s Sustainability Certificate(s) Organizing meetings of the Sustainability Certificate Faculty Working Group and serving as a voting member Overseeing the review of course inclusion proposals Overseeing certificate assessment (in cooperation with the University Sustainability Director and the Associate Director of Assessment) Suggesting changes needed to improve the certificate’s curricula, structure, and/or instructional approaches based on assessment findings and national best practices Coordinating with faculty across campus to grow membership and strengthen the program identity and university-wide commitment Coordinating logistics for program-sponsored events Leading recruiting and retention efforts Guiding the submission of proposed certificate changes to the UCC and, when relevant, the State Board of Education and the university’s institutional accreditor. Helping to organize the annual Sustainability Course Development Workshop and other professional development events for faculty Serving as official advisor for the Sustainability Certificate and relevant “Dept Chair” on Change of Curriculum forms related to the certificate Contingency Description This administrative appointment or the administrative portion of the faculty appointment is temporary. Employee acknowledges and agrees that in the event there is no longer a need for the administrative assignment, as determined by University in its sole discretion, University may change this Agreement and remove the administrative salary and/or course release during the contract year and employee may return to their faculty appointment, upon 60 days written notice. Teaching & Advising TBD Scholarship & Creative Activity TBD Outreach & Extension TBD University Service & Leadership 25 Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Required Qualifications University of Idaho tenure track or non-tenure track associate professor or higher with a terminal degree in their disciplinary field and experience relevant to sustainability Experience working in interdisciplinary activities. Preferred Qualifications Experience proposing new courses or curricula. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 09/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by 10/15/2026 will receive first consideration. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Letter of Qualification Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
