    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52963": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty - Computer Science",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Regular Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Regular Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001452P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Regular Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Engineering Primary Unit Computer Science Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Regular Faculty Position Control Number 2227 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Department of Computer Science invites applications for a full-time, academic-year, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Computer Science, Cybersecurity or Artificial Intelligence to start in August 2027. The successful candidate will establish a strong, independent, externally funded research program and maintain a record of high-quality scholarly publications. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses, mentoring M.S. and Ph.D. students, contributing to curriculum and program development, and participating in departmental, college, and university service. Candidates should demonstrate strong research potential, effective teaching and communication skills, and a commitment to graduate education and student success. Interdisciplinary research, external collaboration, and engagement with industry and government partners are encouraged. Unit/Department Summary Department of Computer Science and Cybersecurity | University of Idaho Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 50% Scholarship & Creative Activity 45% Outreach & Extension 0% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Earned Ph.D. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field by the position start date. Evidence of research in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field, demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications or accepted scholarly work. Evidence of teaching experience, such as serving as an instructor, teaching assistant, guest lecturer, or other documented instructional role in a relevant field. Evidence of written and oral communication experience with academic, technical, or professional audiences. Evidence of collaborative experience in research, teaching, or other academic or professional activities. Preferred Qualifications Strong record of high-quality peer-reviewed publications in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a related field. Demonstrated potential to establish an independent, externally funded research program. Experience pursuing, participating in, or contributing to externally funded research. Experience or demonstrated potential to mentor and advise M.S. and Ph.D. students and engage undergraduate students in research. Evidence of effective university-level teaching or demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching. Experience developing or contributing to undergraduate or graduate courses and curricula. Experience or interest in interdisciplinary and collaborative research. Experience supporting student academic growth, professional development, and achievement. Experience or demonstrated potential to use innovative, hands-on, project-based, or experiential instructional methods. Ability to secure a U.S. security clearance Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open until filled with a first review date of October 29, 2026. Complete applications include: Letter of qualification CV Statement of Research Statement of Teaching List of 3 references Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Transcripts Letter of Qualification Statement of Research Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
