    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52958": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty - Computer Science",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001451P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Faculty Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience Location Moscow Primary Division/College College of Engineering Primary Unit Computer Science Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 2926 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1 Contract Basis Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary The Department of Computer Science invites applications for two full-time, academic-year, non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor positions in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or Artificial Intelligence to begin in August 2027, with the potential to begin earlier. The positions emphasize high-quality teaching, student engagement, and experiential learning at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Responsibilities include teaching lectures, laboratories, and project-based courses in in-person, online, hybrid, and multi-campus formats; contributing to curriculum development, academic advising, outreach, and service; and supporting applied research or industry collaboration. Candidates should demonstrate excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to student success and mentorship. Practical industry experience, professional certifications, and applied research interests are highly valued. Unit/Department Summary Department of Computer Science and Cybersecurity | University of Idaho Administrative Summary Contingency Description Teaching & Advising 90% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 0% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications An earned M.S. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field. Experience in written and oral communication. Experience working collaboratively. Experience teaching courses in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or related experience. Preferred Qualifications An earned Ph.D. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field. Demonstrated excellence in university-level instruction. Demonstrated experience supporting student growth and academic development and achievement. Demonstrated ability to successfully mentor and advise undergraduate students. Demonstrated interest and potential in pursuing and/or supporting research and scholarship activities. Interest in pursuing and supporting research and scholarship activities Demonstrated potential for learning and implementing innovative hands-on instructional methods. Demonstrated potential for delivering instruction in a variety of formats including, but not limited to, local, online, hybrid, hands-on, and laboratory. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants First consideration will be given to complete application packets received by October 15, 2026. Complete application packets consist of: CV, letter of qualification, transcripts, contact information for 3 references, and statements of teaching. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. Uncertain Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Transcripts Letter of Qualification Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently authorized to work in the United States of America? Yes No * Do you now, or in the future require sponsorship through the University of Idaho to continue working in the United States? Yes No University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
