    "https://uidaho.peopleadmin.com/postings/52232": {
      "title": "Clinical Psychologist &amp; PsyD Program Faculty - Department of Health Professions",
      "description": "University of Idaho Job Applicant Portal | Clinical Psychologist &amp; PsyD Program Faculty Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Clinical Psychologist & PsyD Program Faculty Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F001424P Internal Posting? Recruitment Title Clinical Psychologist & PsyD Program Faculty Advertising Pay Range $86,500 annually or more, depending on experience and education Location Moscow Primary Division/College School of Health and Medical Professions Primary Unit Department of Health Professions Employee Category Faculty Classification Group Title Clinical Faculty Position Control Number 6215 Suffix 00 Contingency Code Not Applicable FTE 1.0 Contract Basis Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 05/11/2026 FLSA Status Exempt Tenure Tracking Non-Tenure Track Rank Assistant Professor Extension Type Not Applicable Administrative Appointment Type Not applicable Administrative Appointment End Date (if applicable) Position Responsibilities Position Summary This non-tenure-track clinical faculty position is a 1.0 FTE joint appointment shared equally between the Department of Health Professions in the School of Health and Medical Professions ( SHAMP ) and the University of Idaho Counseling and Mental Health Center ( CMHC ). The faculty member will hold the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor, with an academic home in the Department of Health Professions and will be eligible for promotion to Clinical Associate Professor and Clinical Professor in accordance with university policy. The position includes a 50% commitment to teaching, supervision, scholarship, and related faculty responsibilities in support of the Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) program and a 50% commitment to direct clinical service at CMHC . The faculty member will serve as core faculty in the PsyD program, consistent with APA Commission on Accreditation (CoA) definitions. The faculty member’s academic home will be in the Department of Clinical Medicine within the School of Health and Medical Professions. For matters related to teaching, scholarship, and faculty evaluation, the faculty member will report to the Department Head of Clinical Medicine or their designee. For clinical operations and day-to-day service responsibilities at the Counseling and Mental Health Center ( CMHC ), the faculty member will work under the direction of the CMHC Director or their designee. As a joint appointment, performance evaluations will incorporate input from both units. Clinical faculty positions at the University of Idaho are non-tenure-track and are designed for professional disciplines with strong applied and clinical components. Responsibilities may include teaching, advising, scholarly activity, graduate committee service, and community or professional outreach. Unit/Department Summary https://www.uidaho.edu/cogs/shamp https://www.uidaho.edu/student-resources/health-wellness/counseling-mental-health-center Administrative Summary N/A Contingency Description N/A Teaching & Advising 40% Scholarship & Creative Activity 5% Outreach & Extension 50% University Service & Leadership 5% Qualifications Minimum Education/Degree Required Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology or closely related field from an accredited institution. Licensed or License eligible as a clinical psychologist in the State of Idaho Documented training and supervised experience in evidence-based psychological interventions, including a minimum of one year (or equivalent) of applied clinical practice. Documented training and experience in psychological assessment, including administration, scoring, and interpretation of commonly used standardized instruments. Experience teaching and mentoring students, demonstrated through at least one year of graduate-level instruction, supervision, teaching assistantship, or comparable instructional experience in psychology or a related field. Experience delivering clinically effective and ethically sound services, supported by a minimum of one year of direct service experience with college students or a comparable population. Experience with writing and verbal communication skills, demonstrated through professional reports, presentations, or other formal communication products. Experience collaborating across academic and clinical settings, with evidence of interdisciplinary teamwork or coordinated service delivery. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in a university counseling center, college mental health setting, or similar integrated training environment. Experience with crisis intervention, outreach, consultation, and brief model therapy. Experience teaching doctoral or graduate students in psychology or a related health profession. Experience supervising practicum students, interns, or other clinical trainees. Experience mentoring dissertation or other student scholarly work. Familiarity with APA accreditation standards, doctoral training, or competency-based clinical education. Knowledge of FERPA , HIPAA , risk management, and documentation standards relevant to higher education clinical settings. Experience conducting psychological assessments, evaluating for autism spectrum disorder, ADHD , and learning disorders. Physical Requirements & Working Conditions Posting Information Posting Date 05/06/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants who apply before June 6, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Applicant Resources https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/careers/applicant-resources Background Check Statement Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check. EEO Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. A visa sponsorship is available for the position listed in this vacancy. No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter/Letter of Application List of References Statement of Teaching Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Academic Careers Association of Public and Land Grant Universities (APLU) Chronicle Facebook HigherEd/Academic Impressions Higher Ed Jobs Idaho Department of Labor/Job Service including Job Central or Idaho Works (Idahoworks.gov) Indeed.com Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Newspaper Other Venue Professional Listservs (Ex: NACUBO, AAAE, ISMC, etc.) University of Idaho Website University of Idaho Daily Register University of Idaho Employee Word of Mouth Militaryjob.com DSPSjobs.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) * Were you referred to this employment opportunity by a current University of Idaho employee? If so, please provide their name and department. (Open Ended Question) University of Idaho Human Resources Moscow, ID 83844-4332 (208) 885-3638 employment@uidaho.edu Back to top Copyright © University of Idaho To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
