    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/instructional-laboratory-coordinator-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Instructional Laboratory Coordinator",
      "description": "Instructional Laboratory Coordinator - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Instructional Laboratory Coordinator 492401 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 26 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Division/College: 3984-COS College of Science Department: 880-COS Physics Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $55,000 annually Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: False FLSA Status: Exempt Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Required Experience: Experience working with laboratory equipment Required Education: Bachelor’s Degree in Physics, Mechanical Engineering or a related technical field Required Other: none Additional Preferred: Masters degree or higher in Physics, Mechanical Engineering or a related technical field Experience in design and assembly of laboratory apparatus Experience in operating, troubleshooting and repairing laboratory equipment Experience managing personnel Strong interpersonal and communication skills Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must be able to lift, carry and/or otherwise move up to 50 lbs Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special 