    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/general-technician-i-ii-or-iii-auxiliary-services-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services",
      "description": "General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services 492463 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Nov 4 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: General Technician I, II or III Auxiliary Services Division/College: 3970-AUX Auxiliary Services Department: 907-AUX Campus Services Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: General Technician I $17.19 per hour or higher depending on experience. General Technician II $19.78 per hour or higher depending on experience. General Technician III $22.35 per hour or higher depending on experience. Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: General Technician I This position will perform general building maintenance tasks on a regular and continuing basis. It will provide general support for a variety of construction, trades, landscaping, exterior service and maintenance areas to repair and maintain university facilities and grounds. Job duties will vary widely depending on the work and projects assigned. Duties may include: Utilize basic tools and equipment Repair and maintain basic machinery, equipment and facility property Assist with routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Assist with inventory and distribution of deliveries Manually move and transfer items Participate in snow removal Other duties as assigned General Technician II This position independently performs semi-skilled maintenance and repair duties that vary widely depending on the work and projects assigned. It is responsible for inspecting, maintaining and repairing university equipment and facilities. The position will provide support for construction, maintenance and other skilled trade professionals to meet university needs. Duties may include: Perform routine maintenance and repairs to university facilities Assist trades, crafts, vendors and technical staff with construction, design and operational maintenance as needed Repair and maintain machinery, equipment and facilities Perform routine and non-routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Receive, inspect, inventory and distribute deliveries independently to appropriate entities Other duties as assigned General Technician III This position provides leadership to the General Technician team, which performs semi-skilled maintenance and repair duties for university facilities and equipment on and near the Moscow campus. The work of the team varies widely depending on the work and projects assigned. The position is responsible for planning, organizing, training and monitoring the team’s daily work activities while also performing inspection, maintenance and repair duties. Duties may include: Hire, train and supervise the General Technician team Monitor and balance workload among individual technicians Perform routine maintenance and repairs to university facilities Assist trades, crafts, vendors and technical staff with construction, design and operational maintenance as needed Repair and maintain machinery, equipment and facilities Perform routine and non-routine facility inspections and monitor cleanliness Receive, inspect, inventory and distribute deliveries independently to appropriate entities Other duties as assigned Required Experience: General Technician I Working in a team to accomplish goals General Technician II Three years performing semi-skilled maintenance tasks General Technician III Five years performing semi-skilled maintenance tasks in custodial, landscape, construction and/or utilities trades Required Education: General Technician I, II, and III High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other: General Technician I, II, and III Possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Be at least 18 years of age Ability to participate in a 24/7 on-call rotation which may include nonstandard business hours including evenings, weekends and holidays periodically Additional Preferred: General Technician I Experience: Working in construction or building maintenance Using power tools and equipment Expressed interest in learning and acquiring skills related to building maintenance General Technician II Experience With heating and cooling system maintenance and repairs With basic components and functions of electrical systems, plumbing systems, heating ventilation systems, roofing systems, security lock systems and mechanical systems in residential type dwellings Installing carpet, sheet vinyl, luxury vinyl plank and/or ceramic tile Post-secondary education and/or license in one or more of the following areas: plumbing, electrical or HVAC General Technician III Experience With heating and cooling system maintenance and repairs With basic components and functions of electrical systems, plumbing systems, heating ventilation systems, roofing systems, security lock systems and mechanical systems in residential type dwellings Installing carpet, sheet vinyl, luxury vinyl plank and/or ceramic tile Post-secondary education and/or license in one or more of the following areas: plumbing, electrical or HVAC Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: General Technician I, II, and III Must be able to: Bend, stoop and work in awkward positions for several hours at a time Climb and work from ladders, scaffolding and scissor lifts Carry, lift or otherwise move items weighing up to 50 pounds Stand and walk continuously throughout the workday Work in inclement weather conditions Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification and current resume no later than November 18, 2026. In your letter of qualifications ( https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/applicant-resources) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of hire Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fbba1df6 Last Name (required) 45a8d8a2 Email (required) 1a4a7cd1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 838f6061 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Facilities & Maintenance Facilities & Maintenance Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 77cec135 Last Name (required) 4659cd64 Email (required) a8138f1c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website 