    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/psychologist-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Psychologist",
      "description": "Psychologist - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Psychologist 492478 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Nov 4 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Psychologist Division/College: 3960-SA Student Affairs Department: 743-SA StudBenefits Health Wellness Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $85,000 or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: False FLSA Status: Exempt Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: The successful candidate will join a multidisciplinary team and spend the majority of their time providing direct clinical services to students which includes initial appointments, crisis intervention, individual counseling and psychological assessments within the Counseling and Mental Health Center’s (CMHC) established clinical model. The CMHC offers a broad range of clinical services which include group counseling, psychological assessment, alcohol and other drug programming, biofeedback and trauma-informed treatments. In addition, the psychologist will design and implement educational outreach programs, provide consultation about psychological issues to the campus community, serve in at least one liaison role to a campus partner, provide clinical supervision and training for doctoral interns in the APA-accredited internship program and respond to critical campus incidents or outreach requests. Required Experience: Experience providing clinical services to adults Experience providing risk assessment and crisis interventions Experience working with a multidisciplinary team in a fast-paced and dynamic work environment Required Education: PhD or PsyD in Counseling/Clinical Psychology from an APA Accredited Program Required Other: Eligibility for licensure as a psychologist in the State of Idaho within one year of hire Ability to work nonstandard business hours which may include evenings, weekends and holidays Additional Preferred: Experience providing comprehensive psychological assessment with adults evaluating for Attention-Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder, Learning Disorders, and/or Autism Spectrum Disorder Experience working with individuals impacted by alcohol or other drug use, particularly in early adult populations Experience working with biofeedback Certified or significant training in Dialectical Behavior Therapy (DBT) Strong clinical skills, interest, and experience providing psychotherapy to a student population Professional skills and commitment to working with students, colleagues, and stakeholders Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: None Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered your “Letter of Qualification” must address each of the required qualifications. Additionally, please provide information in support of your application regarding the preferred qualifications as relevant. For 1st consideration, please apply by September 10, 2026 Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of application Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 73c01b67 Last Name (required) ac9c1e17 Email (required) 46fd9c5d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 7770190f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Affairs Student Affairs Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 31197545 Last Name (required) 1b8d16fc Email (required) 76a68279 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Stateme