    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/custodian-i-moscow-idaho-united-states-acd9e756-c0d3-47e6-acee-b40c08777797": {
      "title": "Custodian I",
      "description": "Custodian I - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Custodian I 492457 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Nov 4 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Custodian I Division/College: 3970-AUX Auxiliary Services Department: 907-AUX Campus Services Location: Moscow Location Details: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $16 per hour or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: The position is responsible for maintaining clean and orderly facilities for students, faculty, staff and visitors. As part of a self-directed team, the position will take initiative to schedule cleaning and maintenance activities. Duties may include: Perform basic cleaning, sanitization and trash collection in and around residences halls and university buildings Maintain cleaning equipment and supplies Notify occupants of cleaning and floor maintenance schedules Maintain clean and clear walkways, ensuring they are free of debris, litter, snow and ice Respond to emergencies and assist other departments when needed to ensure optimum service Ensure that assigned rooms and buildings are opened and locked as scheduled Assist with training new employees Other duties as assigned Required Experience: Performing cleaning tasks Working in a team-oriented environment Required Education: None Required Other: Possess a valid driver's license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Be at least 18 years of age Additional Preferred: Experience operating industrial high-speed cleaning equipment; performing minor maintenance on custodial equipment; and explaining the use and maintenance of custodial equipment Expressed interest in learning and acquiring skills related to custodial services Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must be able to: Climb ladders, bend and stoop Lift, carry or otherwise move items weighing up to 50 pounds Stand and walk continuously throughout the workday Work in inclement weather conditions Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: Hiring multiple positions on swing and dayshift. To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification, current resume, and references (last 3 supervisors) no later than November 18, 2026. In your letter of qualifications ( https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/applicant-resources ) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: N/A - no degree required Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 31579281 Last Name (required) d1b9d996 Email (required) 76fb5a20 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 51071682 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Facilities & Maintenance Facilities & Maintenance Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) dc1215b7 Last Name (required) 632b5548 Email (required) dd6f1e4c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable acco