    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/clinical-faculty-moscow-idaho-united-states-02c063e1-75f5-4c04-9b84-df939515b422": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Clinical Faculty 492446 Moscow, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Oct 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College College of Engineering Department Computer Science Position Classification Clinical Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Location Moscow FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary The Department of Computer Science invites applications for two full-time, academic-year, non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor positions in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or Artificial Intelligence to begin in August 2027, with the potential to begin earlier. The positions emphasize high-quality teaching, student engagement, and experiential learning at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Responsibilities include teaching lectures, laboratories, and project-based courses in in-person, online, hybrid, and multi-campus formats; contributing to curriculum development, academic advising, outreach, and service; and supporting applied research or industry collaboration. Candidates should demonstrate excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to student success and mentorship. Practical industry experience, professional certifications, and applied research interests are highly valued. Teaching & Advising Effort 90% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 5% Outreach & Extension Effort 0% University Service & Leadership Effort 5% REQUIRED EDUCATION An earned M.S. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field. REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Experience in written and oral communication. Experience working collaboratively. Experience teaching courses in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or related experience. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE An earned Ph.D. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related field. Demonstrated excellence in university-level instruction. Demonstrated experience supporting student growth and academic development and achievement. Demonstrated ability to successfully mentor and advise undergraduate students. Demonstrated interest and potential in pursuing and/or supporting research and scholarship activities. Interest in pursuing and supporting research and scholarship activities. Demonstrated potential for learning and implementing innovative hands-on instructional methods. Demonstrated potential for delivering instruction in a variety of formats including, but not limited to, local, online, hybrid, hands-on, and laboratory. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS NA POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Contingency on Appointment No Special Instructions to Applicants First consideration will be given to complete application packets received by October 15, 2026 . Complete application packets consist of: CV, letter of qualification, transcripts, contact information for 3 references, and statements of teaching. Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho is supported in limited circumstances from existing visa holders. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment Uncertain Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d0198d46 Last Name (required) c6e87140 Email (required) 92118309 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laborato