    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/regular-faculty-moscow-idaho-united-states-809cd49c-b469-47d6-988a-ce187e65630d": {
      "title": "Regular Faculty",
      "description": "Regular Faculty - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Regular Faculty 492433 Moscow, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Oct 26 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College College of Science Department Biological Sciences Position Classification Regular Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Status Tenure Track Location Moscow FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with experience and qualifications FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/16/2027 POSITION OVERVIEW Primary Faculty Position Summary The Department of Biological Sciences invites applications for a full-time, academic year, tenure-track Assistant Professor position. We seek a highly collaborative scientist to establish a productive, extramurally funded research program in genetics or genomics. The successful candidate will build upon existing departmental strengths and align with our strategic priorities. Duties include teaching an average of 1.5 classes per academic year in the medical sciences curriculum or other programs to meet the teaching needs of the department; maintaining an active research program that includes securing external funding to support research activities in area of expertise; developing research collaborations across the college and university; mentoring undergraduate and graduate students; attending faculty meetings and departmental seminars; serving on department, college, and/or university committees. The Department of Biological Sciences offers undergraduate (Biochemistry; Bioinformatics; Biology; Medical Sciences; Microbiology) and graduate (Biology; Microbiology, Molecular Biology and Biochemistry (MMBB); Neuroscience) degrees. Faculty also participate in the Bioinformatics and Computational Biology interdisciplinary graduate program. The department hosts a supportive and collaborative community of researchers with internationally recognized strengths in evolutionary biology, microbiology, host–microbe interactions, genetics and genomics, cellular and molecular biology, ecology, and computational biology. Faculty benefit from numerous opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration within the department and across the university. Teaching & Advising Effort 35% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 55% Outreach & Extension Effort 5% University Service & Leadership Effort 5% REQUIRED EDUCATION An earned doctorate in genetics, biological sciences, or a closely related field. REQUIRED EXPERIENCE A minimum of 2 years of post-doctoral research experience in an area relevant to proposed research program. An active research program or area of research expertise in a field of genetics or genomics. Experience publishing peer-reviewed work in scientific journals. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE A demonstrated potential to secure external research funding (e.g., grants, fellowships). Documented evidence of experience in college-level instruction. Experience mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate student researchers. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS N/A POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Contingency on Appointment No Special Instructions to Applicants This position is open until filled with a priority review date for those who apply by September 20, 2026 . Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment No Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 237d20a5 Last Name (required) d383b109 Email (required) 14f18cd6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert f1231d5d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Sciences Faculty Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 52d9d671 Last Name (required) 91f4df04 Email (required) 9699f5b4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
