    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/administrative-specialist-i-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist I",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist I - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Administrative Specialist I 492403 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 26 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Administrative Specialist I Division/College: 3977-VPDL Vice Provost for Digital Learn Department: 901-VPDL Vice Provost for Digital Learn Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $19.50 or higher depending on education and experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: Assist with administrative tasks including preparing correspondence, maintaining records, maintaining calendars, monitoring office inventory, ordering supplies when necessary and completing various assignments as needed. This position may be the first point of contact for the department, and is tasked with ensuring that information flows accurately, efficiently and effectively while maintaining appropriate confidentiality. Duties may include: Manage records and documents Perform general administrative support tasks such as proofreading and receiving and distributing mail; may handle cash Greet visitors, callers and/or email inquiries, determining nature and purpose and directing them to specific destinations/individuals/information Other duties as assigned Required Experience: Organizing tasks to meet deadlines Participating in teams to accomplish shared goals Using computer software and applications for word processing, email, and internet searches Required Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other: none Additional Preferred: Bachelor’s degree in related field OR combination of related education and full-time, working experience to total two years Attention to detail, writing, editing, and communication skills as shown in application materials Experience meeting deadlines, handling pressure, and delivering accurate information to team members and leadership Managing projects independently, learning new skills, quickly, and showing initiative without needing close supervision Analyzing data to make informed decisions, provide recommendations, and solve problems creatively Proficient in Microsoft Office, Adobe Acrobat, and photo editing tools like Photoshop Ability to organize and prioritize a variety of projects and tasks in an effective and timely manner Experience working with faculty, staff, and students in a university office setting Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Ability to sit/stand at a desk for extended periods Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: To receive first consideration, please submit a cover letter, current resume, and references no later than October 19, 2026. In your cover letter, using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like a copy of the full job description, please email jradil@uidaho.edu. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: N/A - no degree required Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 42938594 Last Name (required) ba3db5ad Email (required) 84033ec7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert f3d55729 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative Administrative Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) cf1efe0f Last Name (required) 597cb3a2 Email (required) d72256fd Send Pl