    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/research-associate-ii-irrigation-and-agricultural-water-management-kimberly-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Associate II, Irrigation and Agricultural Water Management",
      "description": "Research Associate II, Irrigation and Agricultural Water Management - Kimberly, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Research Associate II, Irrigation and Agricultural Water Management 492398 Kimberly, Idaho, United States, 83341 Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Research Associate II, Irrigation and Agricultural Water Management Division/College: 3998-CALS Col of Agri Life Sciences Department: 842-CALS Fiscal Administration Location: Kimberly FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $58,011.20 annually or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Exempt Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: Performs research activities and analysis; implements, evaluates and recommends adjustments to research procedures. Responsible for synthesizing and independently preparing results for publication. Works under general supervision with a significant degree of creativity and latitude. May coordinate research operations and the daily activities of junior research personnel. Duties may include: Participate in planning and/or designing of major scientific projects, studies, or applications Plan and conduct research and analysis of scientific data Prepare graphic and narrative reports Interpret test results and comparing with determined standards and limits Perform site inspections and field oversight if field work is required Plan, design, develop, monitor and/or evaluate a distinct portion of a scientific project, study or application Research, design, implement, standardize, and evaluate new procedures Maintain detailed records of results and prepares written reports acceptable to the Principal Investigator and funding agencies Other duties as assigned Required Experience: Two years of research experience beyond receipt of Master’s Degree related to the domain of this position Required Education: Master’s Degree in Agronomy, Soil Science, Agricultural Engineering, Biological Engineering, Water Resources, Environmental Science or a closely related to the domain of this position Required Other: Must have a valid driver’s license and the ability to meet UI requirements for driving university vehicles Ability to travel frequently throughout Idaho and occasional regional or national travel Ability to occasionally work non-standard business hours, especially during peak field seasons Additional Preferred: Ph. D in Agronomy, Soil Science, Agricultural Engineering, Biological Engineering, Water Resources, Environmental Science, or a closely related field Experience conducting independent field-based agricultural or environmental research Experience with experimental design, data collection, statistical analysis and interpretation Experience with agricultural water management, irrigation, soil moisture, evapotranspiration, precision agriculture or related research Proficiency with R, Python, GIS, SQL or similar data analysis and visualization tools Experience managing research projects, datasets and competing priorities Scientific writing experience, including peer-reviewed publications, technical reports or thesis/dissertation work Experience supervising students or research personnel and collaborating with producers, Extension or interdisciplinary teams Experience with agricultural equipment, field instrumentation, remote sensing, UAVs, sensor networks or environmental monitoring technologies Experience serving as PI or Co-PI on extramurally funded research Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Work in office, laboratory, greenhouse and outdoor agricultural environments Ability to lift, carry or otherwise move up to 50 pounds and walk long distances over uneven terrain Ability to bend, kneel, climb ladders and work around machinery, chemicals, insects and variable weather Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications received by October 8, 2026, will receive first consideration. IMPORTANT: To be considered, your “Letter of Qualification” must address EACH of the minimum qualifications, including pertinent education and/or experience. In addition, to improve your ranking during the evaluation process, address as many of the Preferred Qualifications as possible. Information on a resume will not be accepted as a substitute for submitting a Letter of Qualification. In addition to your Letter of Qualification, please also include your unofficial transcripts. Please combine letter and transcripts into one pdf file. If you would like to receive a full position description, please email Heather at hbiersner@uidaho.edu and request that one be sent to you. Visa Sponsorship: Uncertain Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of application Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 4d89fb39 Last Name (required) 12589a11 Email (required) cf4ba5ad Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member