    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/physician-classroom-based-clinical-skills-education-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Physician - Classroom Based Clinical Skills Education",
      "description": "Physician - Classroom Based Clinical Skills Education - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Physician - Classroom Based Clinical Skills Education 492462 Moscow, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College School of Health and Medical Professions Department Department of Health Professions Position Classification Clinical Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Location Moscow FTE 0.125 Advertising Pay Range $15,343 or commensurate with experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 03/16/2025 POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary This is position is a non-tenure, Clinical Faculty position with the rank of Assistant Professor. It is part-time, .125 FTE/5 hrs. per week. These physician faculty will teach medical students in the WWAMI Medical Education Program. Weekly clinical skills workshops with 1st and 2nd year medical students: Lead a group of 5-6 students in clinical simulations emphasizing communication skills, physical examination, and clinical reasoning. Advanced physical exam workshops (i.e. cardiovascular, musculoskeletal, abdominal, etc.) Provide formative feedback on Observed Structured Clinical Exams (OSCE’s) Frequency in the Spring Semester decreases to bi-weekly Other responsibilities may include: Involvement in teaching of students 2 week “Clinical Immersion” experience Faculty Development Staff Meetings Student Interest Group Advising Assisting with student orientation Other duties and tasks as assigned. Teaching & Advising Effort 100% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 0% Outreach & Extension Effort 0% University Service & Leadership Effort 0% REQUIRED EDUCATION A terminal degree (M.D., D.O., or equivalent) REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Board certified or Board eligible Active clinical practice in the area, or ability to obtain by time of hire. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE Experience teaching medical and/or other health professional students. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS N/A POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Contingency on Appointment Yes Contingency Description As a WWAMI faculty member, employee’s salary will be paid based on the 39 weeks of the academic contract year. Employee is responsible for delivering and grading of all courses and activities for the 18 month curriculum which extends slightly past the academic year contract end date. Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by February 14, 2025 will receive primary consideration. Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment No Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 75be446e Last Name (required) dbc3fe00 Email (required) 54a277ab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, the