    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/temporary-faculty-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Temporary Faculty",
      "description": "Temporary Faculty - Boise, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Temporary Faculty 492461 Boise, Idaho, United States Temporary Faculty Opening on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College College of Law Department College of Law Position Classification Temporary Faculty Location Boise FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range $45,000 - $60,000, commensurate with experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Semester Anticipated Contract Start Date 01/04/2027 Contract End Date 05/21/2027 POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary The University of Idaho College of Law seeks candidate for a full-time, temporary faculty position at our Boise location for the Spring 2027 semester. The faculty member will teach courses in Constitutional Law and related courses and will contribute to the College of Law community through mentorship and advising. Teaching & Advising Effort 100% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 0% Outreach & Extension Effort 0% University Service & Leadership Effort 0% REQUIRED EDUCATION Candidates must have a J.D. from an accredited school or the equivalent. REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Experience in Constitutional Law, as demonstrated through relevant legal practice, teaching, or scholarship. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE Post-J.D. practice, clerking, or teaching experience PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS N/A POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by November 16, 2026 will receive first consideration. Required documents for application are: Resume/CV Letter of Qualification addressing whether you satisfy each of the required and preferred qualifications for the position List of three references Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) cb4c2984 Last Name (required) d7861f33 Email (required) 1bae1a7c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 436e4eb3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Law Faculty Law Employment Type Temporary Faculty Temporary Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) c6aff8f6 Last Name (required) 1c607c13 Email (required) cb9aebb6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
