    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/administrative-specialist-ii-alumni-relations-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist II, Alumni Relations",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist II, Alumni Relations - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Administrative Specialist II, Alumni Relations 492455 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Administrative Specialist II, Alumni Relations Division/College: 3911-Constituency Experiences Department: 921-FDN Constituency Experiences Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $19 per hour or higher, commensurate with experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: False FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: The position provides a wide range of operational support to visitors, students and employees, navigating a variety of administrative processes, procedures and cyclical calendars of activities critical to the operation of the unit within the broader university. The primary responsibility is to serve as an administrative process expert and coordinator. The position may serve as first point of contact for the department while also performing administrative functions such as researching information and solving problems for faculty, staff and students, and providing program and/or event assistance. Duties may include: Compose, proofread, edit and distribute a variety of business documents and routine reports Maintain schedules and event calendars Coordinate logistics for regular travel and meetings Collect and organize data, enter information into various electronic systems in accordance with university or department procedure to ensure accuracy and compliance, validate information and resolve conflicts in data Review internal operating procedures and practices to determine whether improvements can be made in areas such as workflow and records management Greet office visitors and respond to incoming calls and email correspondence. Provide information about office services and processes, redirect inquiries to appropriate offices/individuals Manage inventory Other duties as assigned Required Experience: One year performing office support functions such as document or records management, composing or editing and formatting business documents, reception and/or customer service Using computer software and applications for word processing, spreadsheets, email and internet research Balancing a workload of assigned tasks to meet multiple deadlines Required Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other: Ability to work nonstandard business hours, including weekends and holidays Possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Additional Preferred: Experience working in a higher education setting Knowledge of University of Idaho and its procedures and protocol Understanding of financial transactions Strong customer service skills Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and written Ability to use techniques and procedures in program and event development; e.g. managing, coordinating, administrating and providing record keeping Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must be able to bend, twist, climb stairs Ability to lift, carry and/or otherwise move up to 25 pounds as needed for event support and inventory management Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification, current resume, and references (last 3 supervisors) no later than November 16th. In your letter of qualifications ( https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/applicant-resources ) using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of hire Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) bf461035 Last Name (required) 2139571b Email (required) 7bc69142 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert e15fe7ce Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative Administrative Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 3485fa6a Last Name (required) df411a7c Email (required) 64e7a814 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
