    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/ranch-production-assistant-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Ranch Production Assistant",
      "description": "Ranch Production Assistant - Boise, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Ranch Production Assistant 492396 Boise, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Ranch Production Assistant Division/College: 3998-CALS Col of Agri Life Sciences Department: 838-CALS Nancy M Cummings Res Center Location: Salmon, ID FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $16.52 an hour or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: Perform skilled and semi-skilled ranch and farm work in support of livestock care, forage production, irrigation, fencing, weed and pest control, and general agricultural operations. Operate and maintain agricultural equipment, support research activities, maintain records, and complete maintenance tasks necessary to sustain productive ranch and farm operations. Duties may include: Monitor livestock and assist with feeding, health checks, treatments, calving, breeding, pasture rotation, watering, and cattle movement Build and maintain fencing, livestock enclosures, and other ranch infrastructure Perform forage production activities including field preparation, planting, fertilizing, spraying, mowing, cultivating, irrigating, harvesting, storing, and delivering crops and forages Assist with the establishment, maintenance, and harvest of field research plots and support cattle-related research activities Operate and perform routine maintenance on tractors, loaders, irrigation systems, and other agricultural equipment Maintain accurate livestock, crop, irrigation, equipment, and operational records and complete required reports, timesheets, email, and training Other duties as assigned Required Experience: Three years’ experience working in agriculture Experience working with and treating minor medical issues with cattle while in pastures and corrals Experience operating basic farm equipment and assisting with the maintenance of the tractors and trucks Experience working on ranch facilities, including performing duties on machines or horses Required Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other: Must have a valid driver’s license and ability to meet UI requirements for driving university vehicles Additional Preferred: Ability to weld, rope cattle, use a weed sprayer, operate and drive a variety of equipment Ability to effectively communicate with ranch employees, faculty, and staff Experience with a variety of irrigation methods Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must be able to lift, carry, or otherwise move items weighing up to 80 lbs May require working in inclement weather (cold/hot/wet/windy/dusty) Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications received by September 28, 2026, will receive first consideration. In addition to filling out the application, please upload a resume and a cover letter. If you would like to receive a full position description, please email Heather at hbiersner@uidaho.edu and request that one be sent to you. This job posting will hire 2 people. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of application Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 12e5b884 Last Name (required) f0f79e07 Email (required) d0b4cefd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 12ee90d7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Agriculture Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) cf35dc39 Last Name (required) 9ab80c7f Email (required) 6dfce1b8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
