    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/program-specialist-twin-falls-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Specialist",
      "description": "Program Specialist - Twin Falls, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Program Specialist 492394 Twin Falls, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Program Specialist Division/College: 3998-CALS Col of Agri Life Sciences Department: 768-CALS Central District Location: Twin Falls FTE: 0.875 Advertising Pay Range: $25.00 per hour or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: This position performs a complex mix of duties in support of project or program development and delivery. Duties may include: Coordinate office operations Document and tracking program schedules and business cycles Plan and coordinate program meetings and events Support program planning and may assist with the development of operating budgets and/or funding proposals Research and compile information for communications such as talking points, speech scripts and responses to correspondence and presentations Coordinate collection of data and materials for reports and other administrative documents Develop and maintain positive liaison relationships with various offices, customers and stakeholders including internal and advisory boards May assist with budget management and provide support for financial and/or personnel processes Other duties as assigned Required Experience: Three years providing administrative, business operations and/or program support Composing, proofing and editing a variety of documents, using proper grammar and punctuation as demonstrated in application materials Using computer software and applications for word processing, developing spreadsheets, email and internet research Required Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other: Possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university-owned vehicles Ability to travel Ability to occasional work non-standard business hours Additional Preferred: Bachelor’s degree in Food and Nutrition, Dietetics, Public Health, Education or related field Experience gathering and compiling data for reports Experience teaching youth and adult audiences Experience engaging and working collaboratively with individuals, families and communities Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must be able to teach or otherwise provide instruction involving physical activities Must be able to lift, carry or otherwise move instructional materials weighing up to 40 lbs Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications received by October 21, 2026, will receive first consideration. IMPORTANT: To be considered, your “Letter of Qualification” must address EACH of the minimum qualifications, including pertinent education and/or experience. In addition, to improve your ranking during the evaluation process, address as many of the Preferred Qualifications as possible. Information on a resume will not be accepted as a substitute for submitting a Letter of Qualification. If you would like to receive a full position description, please email Christina at Christinaa@uidaho.edu and request that one be sent to you. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: N/A - no degree required Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 6d839094 Last Name (required) faeaf7b2 Email (required) d32ef3af Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 8242e4a8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative Admini