    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/farm-operations-foreman-kimberly-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Farm Operations Foreman",
      "description": "Farm Operations Foreman - Kimberly, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Farm Operations Foreman 492395 Kimberly, Idaho, United States, 83341 Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Farm Operations Foreperson Division/College: 3998-CALS Col of Agri Life Sciences Department: 769-CALS Kimberly Research Center Location: Kimberly FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $24.79 per hour or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: True FLSA Status: Classified Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: This role manages all field, equipment, and operational aspects of the University of Idaho’s Kimberly Research and Extension Center (KREC in the Magic Valley. This position is essential to supporting high-quality research projects and the overall mission of the Center, which focuses on agricultural research in crops like potatoes, sugar beets, dry beans, and more. Duties may include: Hiring, training, and supervising farm staff Managing complex plant production protocols for research Maintaining vehicles and equipment Coordinating daily field operations Operating tractor and other equipment Other duties as assigned Required Experience: Two years of experience supervising in an agricultural setting Four years of agricultural experience Experience in: working in a team environment to accomplish shared goals following safety practices keeping records irrigated farming farm management techniques, including equipment operation, maintenance, and crop management practices Required Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Required Other: Must have a driver’s license and ability to meet requirements for driving university vehicles Possess a limited (private) pesticide applicator’s license and chemigation applicator’s license or the ability to obtain these licenses within three months Ability to work nonstandard business hours, including weekends and holidays Additional Preferred: Degree in agriculture, agronomy, mechanics, or related field Knowledge of the requirements of field research Experience running, troubleshooting, and affecting minor repairs of farm equipment, tools, and machinery Knowledge of proper chemical application safety procedures Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Must be able to: Work in adverse environmental conditions and with toxic chemicals Sit for long periods of time in a tractor Climb ladders, bend, and stoop Lift, carry, or otherwise move items weighing up to 75 pounds Stand and walk continuously throughout the workday Work in inclement weather conditions Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications received by October 13, 2026, will receive first consideration. If you would like to receive a full position description, please email Heather at hbiersner@uidaho.edu and request that one be sent to you. In addition to filling out an application please provide a resume and cover letter. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of application Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d8a86f1f Last Name (required) 0d6c7d89 Email (required) 1f99f7f8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 6c0f5cc7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Agriculture Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Kimberly, Idaho, United States Kimberly, Idaho, United States First Name (required) f945e65e Last Name (required) 189c59dd Email (required) 037d44dd Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Oppo