    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/assistant-director-for-employer-relations-outreach-and-development-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development",
      "description": "Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development 492392 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development Division/College: 3964-SEM Strategic Enrollment Management Department: 615-SEM Career Services Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $55,000 or higher depending on education and experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: False FLSA Status: Exempt Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: Serving on the Career Services Leadership Team, the Assistant Director for Employer Relations: Outreach and Development is responsible for developing and maintaining partnerships with state, regional, national, and international employers to increase internships, professional experiences, graduate school, and career opportunities for UI students and graduates. The Assistant Director works with the Career Services Director, Employer Relations staff, and UI branch center directors to accomplish the following, aligning this work with the workforce and educational needs of Idaho’s employers and students: Create and implement a plan for relationship-building with employers in Idaho and the Northwest that offer professional experiences, graduate school pathways, and career positions related to UI majors and degree programs Develop and implement strategies to increase connections and networking opportunities between students and employers Assist employers in expanding their internship programs and accessing qualified internship candidates The Assistant Director also leads the department’s fundraising and development efforts through Career Services’ Distinguished Employer Partnership Program (DEP), and leads the department’s assessment plan by collecting employer outreach data and writing reports and recommendations based on that data. Required Experience: Two years professional experience working in recruitment, human resources, talent management or other related experience One year of professional experience in event planning or development/fundraising Experience with program planning and implementation Experience providing presentations to small and large groups Required Education: Bachelors degree Required Other: Must be eligible for membership in relevant professional organizations Ability to work nonstandard hours including a flexible schedule during select mornings, evenings and weekends to address event needs Ability to travel regionally, in-state and out-of-state on a periodic basis Additional Preferred: Education: Master’s degree E xperience: Professional work experience in a university career services office or employer relations role Managing career services database systems (i.e. Handshake, Symplicity, 12Twenty, CSO, or other job search databases) Technical/computer experience, including the experience using software such as Access, Excel, video conferencing programs (Zoom) and on-line survey programs (Qualtrics, SurveyMonkey, etc. Developing a process for assessment, collecting/analyzing data, and preparing reports and recommendations Skills/knowledge/Ability to: Demonstrated past success in development/fundraising efforts Strong verbal and written communication skills Ability to work effectively both as part of a team and independently to complete tasks Strong organization skills Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: none Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: This position is posted as open until filled, however, applications submitted on or before September 17, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Position will remain open until a suitable pool of candidates is identified. Applicants: Please use your letter of qualification to explain in detail how your work experience, skills, and abilities meet both the required and preferred qualifications as listed in the position description. Your letter of qualification will be used to demonstrate your communication and writing skills to determine your ranking among the other applicants for this position. For resources about how to write a letter of qualification, please visit the HR website here: https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/applicant-resources. Click on the Applicant Documents drop down for a letter of qualifications template. If you would like to view a full copy of the job description, please reach out to the search coordinator at eschirmer@uidaho.edu Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of hire Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ecdab274 Last Name (required) 051c3fa8 Email (required) cf51816e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert b58b5e33 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Advising & Student Support Advising & Student Support Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) dd14fb25 Last Name (required) 12b867c7 Email (required) 709d4ccb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
