    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/idaho-ffa-executive-director-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Idaho FFA Executive Director",
      "description": "Idaho FFA Executive Director - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Idaho FFA Executive Director 492393 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Idaho FFA Executive Director Division/College: 3998-CALS Col of Agri Life Sciences Department: 850-CALS Dept of Ag Edu Leader Comm Location: Moscow Location Details: Location is TBD FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $75,000 annually or higher depending on experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: False FLSA Status: Exempt Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: Provide leadership and administration to the Idaho FFA chapters and the members of the Idaho FFA Association as part of the University of Idaho, College of Agricultural and Life Sciences. This position serves as an external link with the statewide agricultural community, the University of Idaho, the Idaho FFA Association and the Idaho Division of Career and Technical Education. The position is responsible for the day-to-day management of the FFA Association, outreach to the community, and development and implementation of a communication strategy to meet organizational goals. The primary responsibilities of the position are to effectively implement statewide FFA programs and manage and advise state FFA officers. It is critical that this person carry out all duties in alignment with the FFA mission and the integrated model for agricultural education. The position reports directly to the Agricultural Education, Communications and Leadership Department Head within the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences at the University of Idaho. The position will serve on the Idaho FFA Association Board of Director and implement policies and procedures established by the board. Required Experience: Interacting, influencing and working with internal and external stakeholders Providing customer service to internal and/or external customers Experience prioritizing, organizing, managing time and multitasking Experience analyzing and solving problems Required Education: Bachelor’s Degree Required Other: Ability to work nonstandard business hours including evenings and weekends Ability to travel Additional Preferred: Bachelor’s Degree in agricultural education Master’s Degree Classroom experience as an agricultural education teacher/FFA Advisor preferred 3 years of management/supervisory/leadership development A passion for student leadership development and understanding of the FFA association Fiscally responsible and comfortable making decisions that support the longevity of the association Confident in speaking in front of small and large groups Excellent interpersonal, listening, written and verbal communication skills Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: none Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications received by September 24, 2026, will receive first consideration. IMPORTANT: To be considered, your “Letter of Qualification” must address EACH of the minimum qualifications, including pertinent education and/or experience. In addition, to improve your ranking during the evaluation process, address as many of the Preferred Qualifications as possible. Information on a resume will not be accepted as a substitute for submitting a Letter of Qualification. Please also attach unofficial transcripts with your application materials in a combined PDF file with your letter of qualification. If you would like to receive a full position description, please email Heather at hbiersner@uidaho.edu and request that one be sent to you. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of hire Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fdb749f7 Last Name (required) decf60f1 Email (required) 997b0eef Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done 