    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/assistant-director-student-early-alumni-engagement-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement 492389 Moscow, Idaho, United States Staff Opening on: Oct 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Appointment Information Working Title: Assistant Director, Student & Early Alumni Engagement Division/College: 3911-Constituency Experiences Department: 921-FDN Constituency Experiences Location: Moscow FTE: 1 Advertising Pay Range: $60,000 or higher, commensurate with experience Is this position contingent on work and/or funding: False FLSA Status: Exempt Type of Appointment: Full Fiscal Year Position Overview: This position leads engagement initiatives across the student-to-alumni transition, with a focus on career connection, identity development and long-term community building. The Assistant Director works collaboratively with Alumni Relations colleagues, campus partners and other stakeholders to deliver a cohesive, coordinated and meaningful constituent experience. Duties will include: Design and implement initiatives and programming to drive student and young alumni engagement Develop and support career-focused engagement opportunities Cultivate and maintain relationships with campus partners, faculty, student organizations and alumni volunteers Analyze engagement data and feedback Attend university and community events Supervise staff Perform other duties as assigned Required Experience: Two years of experience in program development, engagement, event planning or relationship management Experience coordinating and executing programs or initiatives Experience working collaboratively with partners or stakeholders Demonstrated organizational and communication skills Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines Required Education: Bachelor’s degree Required Other: Ability to travel Ability to work nonstandard business hours which may include weekends and holidays Must possess a valid driver’s license and be able to meet policy requirements for driving university vehicles Additional Preferred: Demonstrated interest in engagement, events or higher education Demonstrated ability to work independently and contribute strategic ideas Experience in alumni relations, higher education or student engagement Developing programs for students or early career professionals Analyzing participation data and improving programs based on insights Experience in event planning and coordination Supervising staff Physical Requirements and Working Conditions: Ability to lift, carry or otherwise move up to 25 pounds Ability to sit at a desk and work on a computer for long periods of time Posting Information Open Until Filled: True Special Instructions to Applicants: This in-person position is based in Moscow, Idaho and not offering Visa sponsorship. To receive first consideration, please submit a letter of qualification and current resume no later than September 17, 2026. Please include a letter of qualifications in your application. Using details and examples, please address all of the required and preferred qualifications for this position and how your experience and skills align. A letter of qualifications template is located here: https://www.uidaho.edu/human-resources/applicant-resources. Please click into the Applicant Documents drop down to access. If you would like to see the full job description, please contact Christy Day at cday@uidaho.edu. Visa Sponsorship: No Degree Requirement Timeline: Degree required at time of hire Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) baa44cb8 Last Name (required) e1ac94f0 Email (required) 60f1dadc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert cfd52711 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Development, Fundraising and Constituency Experience Development, Fundraising and Constituency Experience Employment Type Staff Staff Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) add4cc7e Last Name (required) 5c06bf8e Email (required) 986db7b1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
