    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/research-assistant-professor-aquaculture-twin-falls-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor - Aquaculture",
      "description": "Research Assistant Professor - Aquaculture - Twin Falls, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Research Assistant Professor - Aquaculture 492450 Twin Falls, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Oct 29 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College College of Natural Resources Department Fish & Wildlife Sciences Position Classification Research Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Location Off Campus Location - Hagerman FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range $72,000 or higher depending on experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 01/04/2027 POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary The Department Fish and Wildlife Sciences (FWS) seeks a non-tenure track Assistant Research Professor with expertise in cold water aquaculture and gastrointestinal physiology to help expand our interdisciplinary research and teaching efforts focused on sustainable aquaculture and hatchery management. The position is a term position contingent of continuation of funding. Teaching & Advising Effort 15% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 75% Outreach & Extension Effort 7% University Service & Leadership Effort 3% REQUIRED EDUCATION Completed Ph.D. in Fish Physiology (or related field such as aquaculture, fisheries science, biological science, veterinary science) REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Experience competing for external funding. Experience collaborating with industry, and publishing research in high-impact, refereed journals. Experience solving problems analytically. Experience communicating orally and in writing. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE Experience working as part of an interdisciplinary research team. Experience with cold water aquaculture, fish physiology, biochemical and -omics analyses, and gastrointestinal function/health. Experience in teaching undergraduate courses and mentoring graduate students. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS N/A POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled No - Search will close November 15, 2026 Contingency on Appointment Yes Contingency Description This appointment is contingent on funding and/or work to support the position. Employee acknowledges and agrees that in the event of insufficient funding and/or work, as determined by University in its sole discretion, University may: (1) change this Agreement by adjusting the employee’s FTE and annual salary throughout the contract year; or (2) terminate this Agreement and employee’s employment prior to the end of the term of appointment, upon 60 days written notice or such lesser amount of notice as the funding or sponsoring agency had to give to the University before decreasing or terminating funding for the employee’s position. Employee further acknowledges and agrees that in the event termination for insufficient funding becomes necessary, the notice provisions of Faculty Staff Handbook 3900B will not apply. Special Instructions to Applicants Appropriate work authorization is required for this position. New H-1B visa sponsorship from University of Idaho is supported in limited circumstances from existing visa holders. Other visa sponsorship may be available depending on the candidate’s eligibility. Please contact the International Program Office at intlemp@uidaho.edu for additional visa eligibility information. Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment Uncertain Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b8b73f99 Last Name (required) 9d9ce6f6 Email (required) 261438a6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 8e3ce2ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to t