    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/extension-educator-bear-lake-county-livestock-agriculture-and-4-h-youth-development-idaho-falls-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Extension Educator - Bear Lake County: Livestock, Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development",
      "description": "Extension Educator - Bear Lake County: Livestock, Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development - Idaho Falls, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Extension Educator - Bear Lake County: Livestock, Agriculture and 4-H Youth Development 492449 Idaho Falls, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Oct 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College College of Agricultural & Life Sciences Department Eastern Extension District Position Classification Extension Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Status Tenure Track Location Off Campus Location - Bear Lake County - Montpelier, Idaho FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with Experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/17/2026 Extension Faculty Type County Extension Educator/Professorial POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary The University of Idaho Extension Eastern District seeks a 12-month, tenure-track Extension Educator with the rank of Assistant Professor for Bear Lake County, providing leadership for multifaceted livestock (50%), agriculture (30%), and 4-H Youth Development (20%) programs. They will collaborate closely with county partners, commissioners, and community organizations to ensure programs meet local needs and align with University and Extension priorities. The position includes conducting scholarly work (5%) and contributing to University leadership and service, including county chair duties (15%). This position receives an annual flat rate administrative stipend of $1,500 for County Chair duties. Teaching & Advising Effort 0% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 5% Outreach & Extension Effort 80% University Service & Leadership Effort 15% REQUIRED EDUCATION Master’s degree from an accredited institution in animal science, agricultural science, Extension education, or a closely related discipline. The degree must be completed by the date of hire. REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Experience providing organizational structure and support for a variety of individuals and groups Experience in adapting research materials for effective oral and written presentations Experience recruiting, teaching, organizing and managing groups Experience using technology for program delivery, reporting and teams-based communication PREFERRED EXPERIENCE Ability to work well in a team and provide effective instruction, support, and marketing for programs Previous experience working in Extension Experience in disseminating results through scholarly outlets Experience with supervising, leading, and mentoring others PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS Work a flexible schedule, including some weekends Must possess a valid driver’s license. Ability to lift, carry and/or otherwise move 50 lbs. POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Contingency on Appointment No Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by July 18, 2026 will receive first consideration. Along with your online application, write a letter of qualification addressing how you meet the required and preferred qualifications listed. In addition, your application materials must include a CV, names & contact information for at least three (3) professional references, and unofficial transcripts. Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment No Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) da0f7bc8 Last Name (required) 0fac965d Email (required) 7cc81904 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 8a80b651 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Agriculture Faculty Agriculture Faculty Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Idaho Falls, Idaho, United States Idaho Falls, Idaho, United States First Name (required) ec05d68d Last Name (required) b9cee88e Email (required) 35e656f3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
