    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-or-associate-professor-of-clinical-psychology-moscow-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Psychology",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Psychology - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor of Clinical Psychology 492448 Moscow, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Oct 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College School of Health and Medical Professions Department Department of Health Professions Position Classification Clinical Faculty Rank Negotiable Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Location Moscow FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range $90,000 annually or higher commensurate with experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Fiscal Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 06/21/2027 POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary The School of Health and Medical Professions (SHAMP) at the University of Idaho invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track clinical faculty position in the Department of Health Professions at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor or Clinical Associate Professor. Rank will be determined based on the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. The faculty member will serve as core faculty in the Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) program and will play an important role in the continued development and delivery of the program’s clinical psychology curriculum, student mentorship, clinical training, and scholarly activities. The successful candidate will have a primary emphasis on teaching graduate courses related to their areas of expertise and clinical scholarship within the PsyD program, as well as providing academic advising, mentorship, professional development, and dissertation support for PsyD students. The faculty member will also provide or support clinical supervision of PsyD students, contribute to active scholarship and creative activity related to their areas of expertise, serve on dissertation and other student committees, and participate in program and university service, including program development and activities supporting APA accreditation. Because the PsyD program is in its early stages of development, the successful candidate will have meaningful opportunities to contribute to curriculum development, clinical training infrastructure, student mentorship and professional development, program assessment, and the continued development of the program’s scholarly and professional identity. The successful candidate will demonstrate broad preparation in clinical psychology along with a clearly defined area of clinical, scholarly, or teaching expertise. Strongest consideration will be given to candidates with expertise in child and adolescent clinical psychology, including pediatric psychology, developmental psychopathology, and/or the evidence-based assessment and treatment of children, adolescents, and families. Candidates with expertise in clinical health psychology or behavioral medicine, particularly integrated behavioral health and collaborative care, will also receive strong consideration. Experience working with rural, underserved, or medically complex populations and an interest in interprofessional education are especially desirable. The successful candidate must be licensed as a psychologist in Idaho or eligible for Idaho licensure and expected to obtain Idaho licensure within one year of appointment. Teaching & Advising Effort 65% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 15% Outreach & Extension Effort 10% University Service & Leadership Effort 10% REQUIRED EDUCATION PhD or PsyD in Clinical or Counseling Psychology from an APA accredited program REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Licensed or eligible for licensure as a psychologist in the State of Idaho. Experience teaching, advising, mentoring and evaluating graduate or professional students. Experience working with students, faculty, clinical partners, and other professional colleagues. Experience communicating with others both verbally and in writing. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE Clinical experience in psychology appropriate to the candidate’s area of expertise. Evidence of a record of scholarly or professional activity appropriate to career stage. Evidence of scholarly or professional engagement in an area relevant to clinical psychology, health service psychology, or the candidate’s area of expertise. Experience teaching graduate students in the field of psychology or a related health professions discipline. Experience with APA Commission on Accreditation (CoA) processes, including program development, self-study, or site review. Experience providing clinical supervision to psychology trainees. Expertise in child and adolescent clinical psychology, pediatric psychology, developmental psychopathology, or evidence-based assessment and treatment of children, adolescents, and families. Expertise in clinical health psychology, behavioral medicine, integrated behavioral health, or collaborative care. Experience working with rural, underserved, medically complex, or integrated healthcare populations. Experience with interprofessional education or collaborative practice. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS N/A POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Contingency on Appointment No Special Instructions to Applicants First consideration given to those applications submitted before January 5, 2027 . In addition to CV and references, please upload a teaching and research philosophy. Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment No Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of application. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 44183368 Last Name (required) 7c982e7c Email (required) a0b93bff Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 9c51562a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 2e911723 Last Name (required) 4828ae9c Email (required) b5329aec Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
