    "https://careers.uidaho.edu/jobs/clinical-faculty-moscow-idaho-united-states-34555327-0178-48bf-a875-e540f4d8eaca": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty - Moscow, Idaho, United States Skip to main content Applicant resources Benefits About Job search My Profile Kiosk mode Clinical Faculty 492445 Moscow, Idaho, United States Faculty Opening on: Oct 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites APPOINTMENT INFORMATION Division/College College of Engineering Department Computer Science Position Classification Clinical Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Location Moscow FTE 1.0 Advertising Pay Range Commensurate with Experience FLSA Status Exempt Type of Appointment Academic Year Anticipated Contract Start Date 08/17/2026 POSITION OVERVIEW Faculty Position Summary The University of Idaho College of Engineering seeks applicants for an Assistant Clinical Faculty member on an academic year appointment in the Department of Computer Science and Cybersecurity. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in computer science and cybersecurity, combining lectures with laboratory, project-based, and experiential learning. Instruction may be delivered locally, online, hybrid, across campuses, and through hands-on laboratory experiences. Candidates with practical industry experience, professional certifications, or applied research interests in cybersecurity are strongly encouraged to apply. Applicants should possess excellent written and oral communication skills and demonstrate a commitment to student success, mentorship, and continuous program improvement. Faculty are expected to contribute to departmental, college, and university service activities and to support the University’s mission of engaged learning and community impact. Teaching & Advising Effort 90% Scholarship & Creative Activity Effort 5% Outreach & Extension Effort 0% University Service & Leadership Effort 5% REQUIRED EDUCATION An earned M.S. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a closely related field. REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Experience in written and oral communication. Experience working collaboratively. Experience teaching courses in Computer Science and Cybersecurity or related experience. PREFERRED EXPERIENCE An earned Ph.D. in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, or a closely related field. Demonstrated excellence in university-level instruction. Demonstrated experience supporting student growth and academic development and achievement. Demonstrated ability to successfully mentor and advise undergraduate students. Demonstrated interest and potential in pursuing and/or supporting research and scholarship activities. Interest in pursuing and supporting research and scholarship activities. Demonstrated potential for learning and implementing innovative hands-on instructional methods. Demonstrated potential for delivering instruction in a variety of formats including, but not limited to, local, online, hybrid, hands-on, and laboratory. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS AND WORKING CONDITIONS N/A POSTING INFORMATION Open Until Filled Yes Contingency on Appointment No Special Instructions to Applicants First consideration will be given to complete applications received by September 6, 2026 . Complete application consists of: CV, Letter of Qualification, Statement of Teaching, Transcripts, List of 3 References. Visa Sponsorship Available for Appointment No Degree Requirement Timeline Listed degree qualification is required at time of hire. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fe1eb1ce Last Name (required) d293df40 Email (required) e77d3286 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Instructional Laboratory Coordinator Moscow Provost Coordinates the day-to-day operation of the Physics Educational Laboratories. Supports graduate teaching labs by guiding graduate teaching assistants (TAs) in effective instructional practices and techniques and ensures laboratory courses have adequate materials and content for instruction. Maintains the facilities, equipment and materials used for lecture demonstrations and laboratory experiments. Outside the academic year, duties could include undergraduate laboratory teaching during the summer session, laboratory exercise revision, preparation of course documents for upcoming academic year, inventory and equipment maintenance and other associated duties. Regular Faculty Moscow Provost The Physics Department at the University of Idaho is seeking to hire one tenure-track faculty member at the assistant professor level. We seek a faculty member who will establish strong research programs in experimental, theoretical, or computational physics that will complement or build on existing strengths within the department and the College of Science. General Technician I, II, or III Auxiliary Services Moscow Finance and Administration The Gen Tech I, II or III position works in Campus Services providing maintenance and building support to their assigned area. This role reports to Campus Services, the largest unit in Auxiliary Services, and works primarily in the residence halls and multi-use facilities (Idaho Student Union Building, ICCU Arena, PF1CU Kibbie Dome and others). This role is critical in providing routine and preventive maintenance and ensuring all buildings under Campus Services are maintained at the highest level for the students, staff, and community members who utilize our services. Background Check Statement: Applicants who are selected as final possible candidates must be able to pass a criminal background check EEO Statement: The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Sign up for job notifications Job Alert 2aecb46b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Faculty Engineering Faculty Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Moscow, Idaho, United States Moscow, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 47f36c2d Last Name (required) 2f0cbe12 Email (required) 5f9e8534 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Idaho is an equal employment opportunity employer, including veterans and individuals with disabilities. Request an accommodation University of Idaho is committed to providing access and reasonable accommodation in our services, programs, activities, education and employment. We encourage all qualified applicants to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Accommodation for job applicants is available during the application and/or hiring process. To request accommodation, please visit the Applicant Resources page. Facebook X Instagram LinkedIn Quick Links Human Resources Request an Accommodation Contact Us © 2026 University of Idaho Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
